#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Generate or check the pinned upstream TLV sender vectors.

Extracts the listed type definitions, macros, sender functions and em_msg_t reader functions
from pinned git objects (`git --no-replace-objects show <pin>:<path>`), compiles them against
shim.hpp with c++ -std=c++17 (senders as free functions, readers as members of the shim's
em_msg_t), runs vectors.cpp and writes two fixtures:
crates/em-msg/tests/data/upstream_tlv_vectors.tsv (senders) and
crates/em-msg/tests/data/upstream_reader_vectors.tsv (readers). The upstream working tree is
never read. A sizeof/offsetof probe of every extracted struct is checked against PROBE_EXPECTED
and recorded in the sender fixture as `# Probe:` lines. The harness output must hold exactly the
cases of expected_case_inputs() and expected_reader_cases(), in their order, with the given
inputs and areas. check_row() and check_reader_row() then check each row's return value and
bytes against a model written independently of the harness.

Exit 0: success; 1: invalid extraction or content, or --check found a stale fixture;
2: usage, I/O (including a missing fixture under --check), git, compiler, harness or probe failure.
"""
